From 8cfe36b8e29ac69e3c6ae37f5949209c16f09fe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:18:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8180x-xiaomi-book-12.4: drop the
 duplicate PCIe2 PERST#

PERST# of the NVMe controller (pcie2@1c18000) is described twice: the
host bridge carries the deprecated perst-gpios and the pcie@0 root port
carries reset-gpios, both for TLMM GPIO 102.

Linux 7.2 added the gpiolib-shared framework, which treats a GPIO
referenced by several firmware nodes as shared and wraps it in a
gpiolib_shared.proxy.N auxiliary device.  Two properties plus the
synthetic reset-gpio reference make three references, so the proxy is
created and qcom_pcie_probe()'s devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "perst")
returns -EPROBE_DEFER until the gpio-shared-proxy module - loaded by
udev from the root filesystem - registers the proxy gpiochip.  On this
board PCIe2 only probes at ~15.4 s that way.

That is merely slow when the root filesystem is on the SD card, but when
it is on the NVMe it deadlocks: the NVMe cannot be enumerated before the
PCIe controller probes and the controller cannot probe before the root
filesystem has been mounted, so the initramfs never finds its root.

Keep only the non-deprecated form recommended by qcom,pcie-common.yaml:
reset-gpios in the pcie@0 root port.  With a single reference plus the
reset-gpio one the GPIO is not considered shared and PCIe2 probes as
soon as its PHY is up.

The ACPI tables agree with the rest of the node (PCI2 is the NVMe
segment, its CLKREQ# is TLMM 176 and the PHY rails are PMIC LDO3_C/LDO5_E,
matching vreg_l3c_1p2/vreg_l5e_0p88); PERST# itself is driven by the PEP
firmware and is not exposed in ACPI.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-xiaomi-book-12.4.dts | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-xiaomi-book-12.4.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-xiaomi-book-12.4.dts
index 4b778dc7d247..c5ce108ffb12 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-xiaomi-book-12.4.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-xiaomi-book-12.4.dts
@@ -771,7 +771,11 @@
 // Both PCIE2 and PCIE3 is dectected on Windows,
 // Lets enable them.
 
-// FIXME: Unknown Pin for PCIE2
+// PERST# is described by the root port's reset-gpios (the non-deprecated
+// binding).  Do not add the deprecated perst-gpios here as well: the same
+// GPIO referenced from both the host bridge and the root port makes 7.2's
+// gpiolib-shared framework wrap it in a shared-GPIO proxy, which then needs
+// the gpio-shared-proxy module -- not available when the rootfs is on NVMe.
 &pcie2 {
 	interrupts = <GIC_SPI 672 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 		     <GIC_SPI 671 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
@@ -790,8 +794,6 @@
 			  "msi6",
 			  "msi7";
 
-	perst-gpios = <&tlmm 102 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-
 	//wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
 	vddpe-3v3-supply = <&vreg_nvme_3p3>;
